+++ b/README.md
@@ -17,3 +17,38 @@ make demo-data  # load sample rows for local browsing
 ```
 
 The API listens on the port given by `PORT`, default 3000.
+
+## Finding a free slot
+
+Rather than retrying a booking until one is accepted, ask which slots are free.
+
+```bash
+# Free slots of one room, at least 60 minutes long
+curl "localhost:3000/rooms/$ROOM_ID/availability?from=$FROM&to=$TO&durationMinutes=60"
+
+# Compare every room that seats at least 8 people
+curl "localhost:3000/availability?from=$FROM&to=$TO&durationMinutes=60&capacity=8"
+```
+
+`from` and `to` are ISO instants and the window may span at most 31 days.
+`/availability` is paginated over rooms and reports each room in the page with
+its `slots`, which is empty when the room is busy for the whole window.
+
+A booking that still clashes returns `409` with the conflicting booking and up
+to three free slots of the requested length within the following week:
+
+```json
+{
+  "error": {
+    "code": "BOOKING_CONFLICT",
+    "message": "Room is already booked for this period",
+    "details": {
+      "conflictingBookingId": "...",
+      "suggestions": [{ "startsAt": "...", "endsAt": "..." }]
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Slots are half-open, `[startsAt, endsAt)`, so a booking may start exactly when
+another ends.
